claimed: intent-russian-rows-fixed — the last of what I owe from the consumer review, and the one where I am the defect. They found all three hazards in my thirty Russian rows. (1) THE PERSON MARKER CARRIES THE CLASS and is one letter: не могли бы ВЫ against не могли бы МЫ, можете/можем/может -- and one of those is not even the same part of speech. (2) TEMPLATE DUPLICATION: eight Requests in three shapes, two of them the same sentence with the object swapped, plus a true near-duplicate pair inside Other. (3) TRANSLATIONESE: rows that are evidence about my English source sentence rather than about Russian. Fix all three, and do NOT simply paraphrase -- a fixture rewritten by the same hand that wrote it keeps the same provenance problem, so what changes must be the SHAPES, and what stays must be defensible as something a person would type. Then re-run the language arm and say whether the numbers moved, because a fixture edit that changes nothing measurable is a fixture edit nobody can check.
